<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       JAWA ION DAMAGE - the owner's LOCKED SPEC D1, 2026-08-08
       (design/Jawa/mods/required_mods.md):

         "SINGLE-TARGET STUN GUN with tiered effect by target class - strongest
          vs pure machines/mechanoids, strong vs droids & vehicles, weakest vs
          flesh people (but still capable of eventually dropping a person with
          sustained/stacked fire). This tiering IS the tactical identity."

       All three tiers now exist, and each is produced by a different mechanism:

         machines / drones     empAmountMachine 60 -> ~1800 stun ticks
         droids & vehicles     empAmountDroid   24 -> ~720 stun ticks
         flesh people          NO stun; the JawaIon_Stun buildup below, which
                               ends in down-alive with zero injuries

       harmsHealth=false / makesBlood=false is the capture-not-kill guarantee
       and applies to every tier.
  ======================================================================== -->

  <!-- 🔴 CORRECTION 2026-08-22, ION_MACHINE_TIER_MISSING_1. The comment that
       used to sit here said we inherit "the flesh-vs-mech resistance gradient"
       from EMP for free. WE DO NOT, and we never did. Read from source:
       StunHandler::CanBeStunnedByDamage whitelists Core DamageDefs BY IDENTITY
       for pawns -

           if (def == DamageDefOf.Stun) return true;
           if (def == DamageDefOf.EMP && !pawn.RaceProps.IsFlesh) return true;
           if (Biotech && def == MechBandShockwave && IsMechanoid) return true;
           if (def == DamageDefOf.NerveStun && !IsMechanoid) return true;
           return false;

       - so `causeStun` below has never stunned a single PAWN of any kind. It is
       kept only because the NON-pawn branch of that method asks nothing but
       `def.causeStun`, which is why turrets and stunnable buildings have been
       taking the ion stun correctly all along.

       MEASURED LIVE 2026-08-22 (observed/2026-08-22/ion_buildup/):
         Mech_Scyther   JawaIon_Damage x13 up to @20   stunned=False, stunTicks=0
         Mech_Scyther   vanilla EMP x1 @20             stunned=True,  570 ticks
         Tribal_Warrior JawaIon_Damage x6 @8           downed, alive, no injuries

       The two tiers that were missing are now applied in C# by
       Source/DamageWorker_IonBuildup.cs, which re-issues the hit as vanilla EMP
       at the amounts below. That route - rather than a direct StunHandler.StunFor -
       is what buys EMPResistance, the adaptation timer that stops a mech being
       perma-locked, and the DisabledByEMP effecter. -->

  <!-- FIXED 2026-08-10. This said ParentName="EMP" and the def was being
       DISCARDED every load: "Could not find parent node named EMP for node
       DamageDef". EMP is a CONCRETE def (defName EMP), and ParentName can only
       reference an ABSTRACT def declared with a Name= attribute. Core's own EMP
       does exactly what we now do: ParentName="StunBase", where StunBase is
       DamageDef Name="StunBase" Abstract="True" in Core Damages_Stun.xml. -->
  <DamageDef Class="JawaIonWeapons.IonDamageDef" ParentName="StunBase">
    <defName>JawaIon_Damage</defName>
    <label>ion</label>
    <deathMessage>{0} was overloaded by ion fire.</deathMessage>
    <harmsHealth>false</harmsHealth>
    <makesBlood>false</makesBlood>
    <explosionColorEdge>(0.55, 0.75, 1.0, 0.85)</explosionColorEdge>

    <!-- WIRED 2026-08-11. Custom worker, see Source/DamageWorker_IonBuildup.cs.
         It calls base.Apply first, so the impact sound and vanilla bookkeeping
         are unchanged. -->
    <workerClass>JawaIonWeapons.DamageWorker_IonBuildup</workerClass>

    <!-- ⚠️ Kept for NON-PAWN targets only - turrets and stunnable buildings.
         It cannot and never could stun a pawn; see the correction above. -->
    <causeStun>true</causeStun>

    <externalViolenceForMechanoids>true</externalViolenceForMechanoids>
    <stunAdaptationTicks>2200</stunAdaptationTicks>
    <impactSoundType>Electric</impactSoundType>
    <combatLogRules>Damage_EMP</combatLogRules>

    <!-- D1's TOP TWO TIERS. EMP-equivalent amounts, not ticks: StunHandler turns
         a point into 30 ticks and then subtracts the target's EMPResistance, so
         an armoured mech resists exactly as it does against a vanilla EMP
         grenade - which lands 20, for 600 ticks. 60 is three times that, which
         is the "nearly one-shot-disable a mech" half of the spec.
         ⛔ Flesh gets NEITHER of these. Its tier is the buildup below. -->
    <empAmountMachine>60</empAmountMachine>
    <empAmountDroid>24</empAmountDroid>

    <!-- D1's BOTTOM TIER, and the capture-not-kill pillar. The worker reads this
         block by hand and applies the severity without ever dealing an injury -
         ~0.24 per bolt at damage 8, so a flesh target collapses alive after
         roughly six solid hits, and decay bleeds it off if fire stops.
         🔴 The "KNOWN INERT" note that used to sit here is STRUCK. It was true of
         the 2026-08-10 def, which had no worker; the worker has read this block
         since 2026-08-11 and the live measurement above proves it fires. -->
    <additionalHediffs>
      <li>
        <hediff>JawaIon_Stun</hediff>
        <severityPerDamageDealt>0.03</severityPerDamageDealt>
      </li>
    </additionalHediffs>
  </DamageDef>

</Defs>
